    {
      "id": "sce-start-team-slides-q-74f5dd87",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "Describe how the team should be presented in a startup presentation, and how that part fits with the rest of the template.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "The template devotes a run of slides to the team, one per member, up to Team member 5.\n\n**Each slide** carries **Department, Contribution, Achievement and Learning**, so the audience learns where each person worked, what they added, what they achieved and what they learned.\n\n**Fit with the rest.** The presentation opens with a title, tag line and an interesting opening, presents the **Solution** (Key Features, Advantage, Benefits), then **Key Achievements**, then the people, and ends with an **Interesting Conclusion**.\n\nIn conclusion, the team slides give the human side of the startup after the solution and achievements have been shown.",
